<BaseLayout title="Disclaimer">
  <div class="disclaimer-page">
    <h1>Disclaimer</h1>

    <section>
      <h2>Educational purpose only</h2>
      <p>
        SecArsenal is an independent, educational reference for information
        security professionals and students. It catalogs publicly available
        penetration-testing operating systems and tools, describes what they
        do, and links to their official documentation and download pages. It
        does not host, bundle, or distribute any of the software it
        describes, and it does not provide exploit code, live attack
        infrastructure, or step-by-step attack instructions against real
        systems.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Authorized use only</h2>
      <p>
        Every tool and operating system referenced on this site is
        dual-use: the same capabilities used in an authorized penetration
        test can cause real harm if used against systems without
        permission. You are solely responsible for ensuring you have
        explicit, documented authorization before using any of these tools
        or techniques against any system, network, or account you do not
        own. Unauthorized access to computer systems is illegal in most
        jurisdictions.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>No warranty</h2>
      <p>
        Information on this site is provided "as is," without warranty of
        any kind. Tool behavior, licensing, and download locations can
        change after our last verification date shown on each page — always
        confirm details against the official source linked from that page
        before acting on them.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>No affiliation</h2>
      <p>
        SecArsenal is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by any
        of the projects, distributions, or vendors it documents. Names,
        logos, and trademarks belong to their respective owners.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
